Things were going really well for Kupopo the Dwarven Valkyrie.  On
Dlvl 3, she found not one, but two altars.  They were cross-aligned,
but after a few sacrifices, she managed to wrest an altar from Odin.
Not long after, a sacrificed kobold pleased Tyr enough to bestow
Mjollnir upon her, which she greatly appreciated and proceeded to use
to cause much havoc.  This was in fact the first time she or any of
her kin had ever seen the legendary warhammer.  While proceeding
through the next few levels, she found some nifty armor, including a
cloak of protection, speed boots, a +1 dwarven mithril coat, and +3
leather gloves, ultimately bringing her AC down to a record -8.  She
breezed through Sokoban, slightly disappointed with the cursed "oR she
found on a were-corpse.  On the way back up, she (telepathically) saw
something quite interesting - in a side room of Dlvl 7 was a blue
dragon.  Very excited about the prospect of some dragon scales,
whatever the color, she sprinted towards it, but before she got there
it had somehow changed into a giant eel, a shark, and finally some
sort of explosive sphere that ended up blowing itself up.  She
searched all around for a polytrap but couldn't ever find anything -
she went to her grave never knowing quite what happened there.

Nevertheless, she continued back up to the Gnomish Mines in hopes for
a bag of holding to alleviate her burdens.  At one point she became
hungry and even weak and prayed to Tyr, forgetting it had only been
800 turns since her last prayer.  Tyr was displeased, and this was the
beginning of the end.  She spent a while with a /oCM next to the
altar, trying desperately to mollify Tyr, but to no avail.
Eventually, finding no other altars in the next few levels below the
Oracle, she devised to head for Minetown and see what sort of altar
she might find there.  The trip through the mines was quite chaotic.
After sensing a mind flayer (and considering how she might find and
lure her pet onto the polytrap that must be somewhere) she quickly
fell into a pit, and then a level teleporter, skipping Minetown
entirely.  Another pit and level teleport later, she found herself in
Mine's End.  She worked her way back up to Minetown, where she finally
found her first sack.  This was at least better than nothing.  She
quickly tamed one of the wandering dogs and found Eaven's ghost in
Loki's temple.  So no luck with the co-aligned altar.  All the shops
in town were pretty much cleared out, but Eaven had a bag of holding
that Kupopo fervently desired.  Dropping it on the altar revealed it
to be cursed, and with no holy water or /oCancellation anywhere, it
didn't look too promising.  Moreover, with Tyr's anger, there was no
holy water in sight in the near future.  She now had the bright idea
that she might convert the Minetown altar, in the hopes of getting
some beefier sacrifices which might placate her god.  With an AC of
-8, she figured the priest shouldn't be too much trouble.  Closing the
door to the temple (so the watchmen wouldn't notice), she proceeded to
drop a golden naga hatchling corpse onto the altar and #offer it.
Indeed, Tyr's power increased, and the priest of Loki was
understandably upset.  He kicks: -1 HP, still okay.  She scores a few
good hits with Excalibur.  He hits: -34, down to 76 HP, a little more
worrisome but maybe it'll be alright.  Another hit for 25.  And then,
he summons a swarm of 5 giant ants and a killer bee, all surrounding
the weakening Kupopo.  As a last-ditch effort, she prays to Tyr, but
finds him angrier than before.  Over the next two turns, the ants bite
and the bee stings and the priest hits, and finally she breathes her
last on the altar.

In hindsight, she probably should have read that ?oTeleport, or maybe
zapped the priest with one of her /oPolymorph.  Lessons: be more
careful of cross-aligned priests.  And watch the prayer timeout more
closely.  And don't try praying until you *know* your god is placated.

